A brand-new approval-subject table with no existing rows: nothing to backfill, nothing to reconcile, and no prior operator mapping loses its meaning. The authority change (free-text approver metadata stops authorizing; a decided Flows gate over this table's digest authorizes) is enforced in engine code at collect, preflight, and apply time, so previously collected rows re-verify under the new rule on their next run instead of migrating under the old one.
